# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 vecteur.cc, solve.cc, misc.cc: the float row reduction under rank, rref, ker, det, inv and linsolve (backlog F436; T6b bug hunt 2026-11-16, G622). Each test below took a float entry for 0 by is_zero (|x| <= epsilon, 1e-12 at any Digits, gen.cc) or for nonzero by is_exactly_zero, whatever the precision and the matrix's scale. (1) vecteur.cc linear_combination, the row operation of mrref's generic path (an MPFR matrix, Digits > 14), zeroes a cancelled entry with trim, which tests doubles only, and rref_reduce's pivot test is is_exactly_zero, so the cancelled pivot of a singular MPFR matrix (about 1e-40 at Digits 40) was a pivot: rank(evalf([[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]])) = 0 (right 2), rref the identity (right [[1,0,-1],[0,1,2],[0,0,0]]), ker [] (right the line through [1,-2,1]), linsolve(…,[1,2,3]) one solution for a line of them. Now an MPFR sum c1*x+c2*y at or below the rounding of its terms, 2^(12-prec) of the larger, is an exact 0, as trim makes it for doubles. (2) mrref divided each line of a float matrix by its largest entry, 1/0 for a zero line (rank(evalf([[0,0],[0,1]])) = 2 at Digits 40); a zero line now stays. (3) is_blockmatrix, under det and inv, split a matrix into blocks at entries is_zero takes for 0, so M = evalf([[10^-13,2*10^-13],[3*10^-13,4*10^-13]]) was two 1x1 blocks: det(M) 1e-13 (right -2e-26), inv(M) [[1e13,0],[0,2.5e12]] (right [[-2e13,1e13],[1.5e13,-5e12]]); now only exact zeros split it. (4) in_doublerref (Digits <= 14) took a first pivot below 1e-13 for 0 whatever the matrix's scale, so M had no pivot at Digits 12 (inv(M) [[infinity,0],[0,infinity]], det 0); now below a scale of 1 (the largest |entry| reduced) the first test scales with it. (5) solve.cc _linsolve took a square matrix as triangular by is_zero, so M was lower triangular: linsolve(M,[1,1]) = [1e13,-5e12] at any Digits (right [-1e13,1e13]); now by exact zeros. (6) mdividebypivot's first_non_zero skipped a pivot below 1e-12 of its row's largest entry and mker took a diagonal entry below 1e-12 for 0, so the kernel of [M|-b] had a wrong dimension (linsolve(M,[1,1]) = [] after (5)); an MPFR entry is now zero there when it is an exact zero. (7) misc.cc _rank counted rows of mrref's result (rows multiplied by the pivots) that are not is_zero, so a matrix whose pivots are below 1e-12 had rank 0: rank(evalf([[1,1],[1,1+10^-20]])) at Digits 40 (right 2); an MPFR entry is now zero when it is an exact zero. Exact matrices, doubles of scale 1 or more and non-singular matrices of moderate scale keep their answers; is_zero and epsilon are not changed.
